Recommends:
 bingux-preview-host (= ${binary:Version}),
 eject,
 gvfs,
 tar,
 udisks2,
 unzip,
 util-linux,
Suggests:
 bingux-settings (= ${binary:Version}),
Description: File manager for the Bingux desktop
 Files is the Bingux desktop's file manager. It has tabs, a places sidebar,
 list and grid views, previews, search and file operations with undo. It opens
 folders and bingux-files:// addresses.

Package: bingux-preview-host
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-base,
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-good,
Recommends:
 gstreamer1.0-libav,
 gstreamer1.0-pipewire,
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad,
Description: Helper process that plays media and renders PDFs for Bingux previews
 bingux-preview-host plays audio and video (GStreamer) and renders PDF pages
 (poppler) for the Files preview. It is a separate program so that a damaged
 file crashes it and not the file manager, and so that Files itself links
 neither library. Files finds it beside its own program or on the PATH.

Package: bingux-audio-effects
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 pipewire (>= 1.4),
 libspa-0.2-modules (>= 1.4),
 liblilv-0-0,
 lsp-plugins-lv2,
 systemd,
Recommends:
 pipewire-bin,
 wireplumber,
 calf-plugins,
 zam-plugins,
 mda-lv2,
 x42-plugins,
 rubberband-ladspa,
Description: Sound effects for the Bingux desktop
 bingux-effects puts a stack of effects between applications and the speakers,
 or between a microphone and applications, using PipeWire's filter-chain. The
 effects are the published plugins Easy Effects uses (Linux Studio Plugins,
 Calf Studio Gear, ZamAudio, MDA, x42 and Rubber Band); the package contains
 none of its own. Settings edits the presets and turns the effects on.

Package: bingux-taxonomy
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 fontconfig,
 hicolor-icon-theme,
 libegl1,
 libgl1-mesa-dri,
 libwayland-client0,
 libwayland-egl1,
 libxkbcommon0,
Description: Reference window for the Bingux UI components
 Taxonomy shows every component, icon and design token of the Bingux UI
 library in a running window. It is a development tool for people who build
 Bingux applications; ordinary desktops do not need it.
